    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d847">

                <pb facs="0822" n="810" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg810"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1940: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-01T09:00:00+03:00">September 1,
                            1943—9 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 2—2:06 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1571. For Alling from Hoskins. In connection my cable August 27<anchor n="98"
                        xml:id="d847-f1"/> from Basra Moose cabled from Jidda on August 30 that
                    Yusuf Yassin on Saturday gave Wikeley detailed account of my discussions in
                    Jidda. Moose said he assumed London probably knew results of my visit already.
                    [Hoskins.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
